# Hosts the server kit manages. Copy to hosts.conf (the `server-kit` command does this
# once) and replace these examples. hosts.conf lives in your user config directory,
# never in a repository.
#
# name | ssh target (anything `ssh` accepts; ~/.ssh/config aliases work) | notes
#
# The addresses below are RFC 5737 documentation addresses and example.com names.
web1        | deploy@web1.example.com                       | Ubuntu; nginx + Python app
api1        | -J admin@bastion.example.com admin@192.0.2.10  | reached through a bastion
bastion     | admin@bastion.example.com                     | Amazon Linux / RHEL family
